> is this better or overdoing?

I don't have an opinion from a node maintainer's point of view as I'm not one, though if you want a simpler pure JS version then just using `canParse` is still about 20 times faster than `try/catch` in a quick profile I did.

i.e. Doing something similar to this is faster with no downside compared to the `try/catch` approach:

```js
static parse(url, base=undefined) {
    if (URL.canParse(url, base)) {
        return new URL(url, base);
    }
    return null;
}
```
